              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/orbifold"} orbifold
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/higher+orientifold"} higher orientifold
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fixed+point"} fixed point
            in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ho%C5%99ava-Witten+theory"} Hořava-Witten theory
            might be called it
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/O-plane"} O9-plane
            but is often called the
            %em M9-brane
            (e.g.
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#GKSTY02"} GKSTY 02, section 3
            = succeed ")," do
              %a{:href => "#MoorePeradzeSaulina04"} Moore-Peradze-Saulina 04
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/M2-brane"} M2-brane
            and
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/M5-brane"} M5-brane
          %p
            %a{:href => "#Hull97"} Hull 1997, pages 8-9
            argued that the M9-brane is the object whose charge is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Poincar%C3%A9+duality"} Poincaré dual
            to the time-component of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/M2-brane"} M2-brane
            charge as it appears in the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/M-theory+super+Lie+algebra"} M-theory super Lie algebra
            via
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mo ∧
                    %mn 2
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msup
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mrow
                      %mn 10
                      %mo ,
                      %mn 1
                  %msup
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo *
                  %mo ≃
                  %msup
                    %mo ∧
                    %mn 2
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msup
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mn 10
                  %msup
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo *
                  %mo ⊕
                  %msup
                    %mo ∧
                    %mn 9
                  %msup
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mn 10
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\wedge^2 (\mathbb{R}^{10,1})^\ast
                  \\simeq
                  \\wedge^2 (\mathbb{R}^{10})^\ast \oplus \wedge^{9} \mathbb{R}^{10}
                  \\,.
          %p
            (Analogously, the time component of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/M5-brane"} M5-brane
            charge is argued to be dual to the charge of the
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/KK-monopole"} KK-monopole
            = succeed ".)" do
              %a{:href => "Kaluza-Klein+monopole#OtherBraneCharges"} there
          %p
            Under the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/duality+in+string+theory"} duality
            between
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/M-theory"} M-theory
            and
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/type+IIA+string+theory"} type IIA string theory
            the M9-brane may be identified with the
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/O8-plane"} O8-plane
          %p
            %img{:src => "https://ncatlab.org/nlab/files/O8DualToM9.jpg", :width => "600"}/
          %blockquote
            %p
              from
              %a{:href => "#GKSTY02"} GKSTY 02, section 3
          %p
            This may be used to understand the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/gauge+enhancement"} gauge enhancement
            to
            = succeed "-" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/E8"} E8
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/gauge+groups"} gauge groups
            at the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/heterotic+string+theory"} heterotic
            boundary of
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Horava-Witten+theory"} Horava-Witten theory
          %p
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/files/ViaO8GaugeEnhancementOnM9.jpg", :title => ""} ViaO8GaugeEnhancementOnM9.jpg
          %p
            %img{:src => "https://ncatlab.org/nlab/files/ViaO8GaugeEnhancementOnM9.jpg", :width => "600"}/
          %blockquote
            %p
              from
